Typosquatting, also known as URL hijacking, is a cyber attack in which attackers register domain names that are 
intentionally misspelled versions of popular websites or brands.

In cybersecurity, a hoax refers to a false or misleading claim that is spread via email, social media, or other 
communication channels to deceive users.

Familiarity refers to a psychological principle often exploited in social engineering attacks.

In cybersecurity, intimidation refers to tactics used to scare or pressure a target into taking a particular action, 
often involving threats or high-pressure language.

Urgency is a technique often used in phishing scams and other social engineering attacks, where the attacker creates a 
false sense of urgency in the victim. 
